    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d430">

                <pb facs="0451" n="447" xml:id="pg447"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.943 Manchuria/52</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Belgian Embassy to the Department of
                    State</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-sibling-dates" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1938-02-24T23:59:59-05:00" notBefore="1938-02-23T00:00:00-05:00"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]<anchor n="92" xml:id="d430-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi></p>
                <p>The Belgian Government has taken note of the declaration which the Government of
                    Manchukuo made on November 5, 1937, on the occasion of the signature of the
                    treaty relating to the termination of extraterritoriality between Manchukuo and
                    Japan as well as of the interview which Mr. Chuichi Ohashi gave to the press on
                    the subject of the status of foreign nationals in Manchukuo.</p>
                <p>The Belgian Government cannot admit that the treaty of November 5, 1937, can have
                    as a consequence the abolition in Manchukuo of the privileges of
                    extraterritoriality which Belgian nationals enjoy by virtue of the treaties
                    always in force.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
